    "answer": {
      "short": "$180,\\ 585$.",
      "worked": "Let $a$ and $b$ be the hundreds and units digits. Divisibility by 5 requires $b=0$ or $b=5$.\n\nIf $b=0$, the digit sum is $a+8$. Since $1\\leq a\\leq9$, its only possible multiple of 9 is 9:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+8&=9\\\\a&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThis gives $180$.\n\nIf $b=5$, the digit sum is $a+13$. Its only possible multiple of 9 is 18:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+13&=18\\\\a&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nThis gives $585$. Therefore all such numbers are $180$ and $585$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
